@participant1 

> Is it straightforward for you to test on some more versions, get a closer idea of when the issue came in?

I tested pre-built firmware from the website. V1.18 is the most recent version that passes. V1.19.1 (and later) fail. Hence between January and June 2022. Git blame shows some changes to `spi.c` two years ago.

@reporter @participant1 
I just noticed that reading from SPI works if spi.write_readinto() is used and the write and read buffers are different objects. If the buffers are the same, it fails. And in extmod/machine_spi.c, spi.read() uses the same buffer for read & write:
```
STATIC mp_obj_t mp_machine_spi_read(size_t n_args, const mp_obj_t *args) {
    vstr_t vstr;
    vstr_init_len(&vstr, mp_obj_get_int(args[1]));
    memset(vstr.buf, n_args == 3 ? mp_obj_get_int(args[2]) : 0, vstr.len);
    mp_machine_spi_transfer(args[0], vstr.len, vstr.buf, vstr.buf);
    return mp_obj_new_bytes_from_vstr(&vstr);
}
MP_DEFINE_CONST_FUN_OBJ_VAR_BETWEEN(mp_machine_spi_read_obj, 2, 3, mp_machine_spi_read);
```

1. Doing the same read twice in a row triggers the error twice.
2. The bug triggers for all lengths. With longer reads only the first n bytes may be disturbed, where n varies from attempt to attempt. But we have seen that already before. Example:

```
>>> spi.read(30,0x55);
b'UUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUU'
>>> spi.read(30,0x55);
b'UUUUUUUUUUUUUUUU\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00'
>>> spi.read(40,0x55);
b'UUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUU\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00'
>>> spi.read(40,0x55);
b'UUUUUUUUUUUUUUUU\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x
```

3. Adding some delay before and after the two calls to HAL_DMA_Start_IT() does not help. The error is still present.
